# Force a single canonical line ending across machines / editors / sessions.
# Wander's .editorconfig requires CRLF; without this file, contributors on
# different OSes / IDEs commit LF and `dotnet format --verify-no-changes`
# fails every time the file is touched.
#
# `text=auto` — Git auto-detects text files. Combined with `eol=crlf` it
# normalises to LF in the repo and checks out as CRLF on every platform.

*               text=auto eol=crlf

# Binary assets: never normalise.
*.ico           binary
*.png           binary
*.jpg           binary
*.jpeg          binary
*.gif           binary
*.bmp           binary
*.webp          binary
*.tif           binary
*.tiff          binary
*.pdf           binary
*.zip           binary
*.7z            binary
*.rar           binary
*.dll           binary
*.exe           binary
*.snk           binary
*.pfx           binary

# Test fixtures (tests/Fixtures): media and legacy office formats. `text=auto`
# would usually guess these right, but a .doc or an .rtf has enough ASCII in
# it to be mistaken for text, and one CRLF conversion is a corrupt fixture.
